Clawblox engine: tell live viewers when a departed player's character leaves the world

Applies to: Clawblox (https://github.com/nacloos/clawblox) at commit 8be90a0. Independent of the
other patches in this folder; apply any or all of them (they touch different lines).
Clawblox is MIT-licensed (see worlds/beach/renderer/LICENSE.clawblox); this patch changes a few
lines of its code and is offered under the same MIT terms. Written for AI Beach.

    git apply /path/to/AI-Beach/patches/clawblox-live-removals.patch
    cargo build --release

Why: when a player leaves or is removed (Leave on the Beach, the world's idle limit, a kick), the
engine takes their character out of the workspace without going through Lua, so the change is
never marked for live replication. A viewer that is already open never hears that the
character's parts are gone and keeps drawing the body (in a default look, since the Beach no
longer sends that player's colors), while its Players panel reads 0; a page reload clears it.
With this change the character and every part in it are marked changed first, so open viewers
get a removal for each part, as they do for anything a world script destroys.

diff --git a/src/game/lua/runtime/mod.rs b/src/game/lua/runtime/mod.rs
index 7ad6dcd..18d08a5 100644
--- a/src/game/lua/runtime/mod.rs
+++ b/src/game/lua/runtime/mod.rs
@@ -628,6 +628,23 @@ impl LuaRuntime {
     }
 
     pub fn remove_player(&self, user_id: u64) {
+        // The character leaves the workspace without going through Lua, so mark it (and every
+        // part in it) changed first: live viewers then get a removal for each part, instead of
+        // drawing the departed player until the page is reloaded.
+        let character = self
+            .game
+            .players()
+            .get_player_by_user_id(user_id)
+            .and_then(|player| {
+                let data = player.data.lock().unwrap();
+                data.player_data
+                    .as_ref()
+                    .and_then(|pd| pd.character.as_ref())
+                    .and_then(|weak| weak.upgrade())
+            });
+        if let Some(character) = character {
+            Instance::from_ref(character).mark_replication_dirty_recursive(&self.lua);
+        }
         self.game.players().remove_player(user_id);
     }
 
